==========================================
CLOUD/DEVOPS DAY 06 NOTES — S3 Event-Driven Lambda
Date: 28-11-2026
==========================================

WHAT I LEARNED TODAY:
- A bucket can be wired to automatically call a Lambda function on object events (no manual invoke)
- Three pieces are needed: the function, add-permission (letting S3 call it), and the bucket
  notification configuration (saying which events trigger it)
- The event payload (Records[].s3.bucket.name / .object.key) is built by S3 itself, not by me
- Reused Day 03's IAM role again - the same role works across different Lambda functions
- This is the standard "upload triggers processing" serverless pattern used in real AWS architectures

COMMANDS I PRACTICED:
[ ] awslocal lambda create-function (reusing Day03LambdaExecutionRole)
[ ] awslocal lambda add-permission --principal s3.amazonaws.com
[ ] awslocal s3api put-bucket-notification-configuration
[ ] awslocal s3 cp <file> s3://bucket/   (the trigger itself)
[ ] awslocal logs describe-log-streams / get-log-events (proof it ran)

paste your real output here :
$ awslocal s3 cp trigger-test.txt s3://day06-trigger-bucket/
$ (log output showing the print() line)
